=== SURVEY ===
- energy_repo.go: GetDailyBreakdown and GetTotalEnergy query mv_energy_daily (DROPPED)
- models.go: EnergyStatsRow has DistanceKm (float64, json:distance_km) and Efficiency (float64, json:efficiency)
- energy_service.go: EnergyStats has TotalDistance (json:total_distance_km) and AvgEfficiency (json:avg_efficiency_wh_km)
- energy_handler.go: Two handlers return hardcoded JSON keys total_distance_km, avg_efficiency_wh_km
- signal_history_writer.go: Stats() queries mv_signal_stats (DROPPED), replaced by cagg_signal_hourly
- cagg_fleet_stats columns: vehicle_id, day, drive_count, total_distance_mi, total_energy_kwh, total_regen_kwh, total_duration_min, avg_speed_mph, max_speed_mph, avg_score
- cagg_signal_hourly columns: vehicle_id, signal_name, hour, sample_count, avg_value, min_value, max_value

=== REASONING ===
1. mv_energy_daily was dropped by migration 000142, replaced by cagg_fleet_stats
2. Unit changed: distance_km -> distance_mi (cagg_fleet_stats uses miles from drives table)
3. Efficiency must be computed: total_energy_kwh / total_distance_mi * 1000 = Wh/mi
4. Cost column not available in cagg_fleet_stats — return 0
5. mv_signal_stats was dropped, replaced by cagg_signal_hourly (column renames: signal->signal_name, min_val->min_value, max_val->max_value, avg_val->avg_value, cnt->sample_count)
6. energy_handler.go JSON keys updated to match new unit names

